{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":42148664,"ns":0,"title":"Benacerraf's identification problem","extract":"In the philosophy of mathematics, Benacerraf's identification problem is a philosophical argument developed by Paul Benacerraf against set-theoretic Platonism and published in 1965 in an article entitled \"What Numbers Could Not Be\".  Historically, the work became a significant catalyst in motivating the development of mathematical structuralism.","description":"Argument in philosophy of mathematics","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}